Here's a simple example website for a fake mechanic shop in Detroit using HTML, CSS, JS, and Bootstrap:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>DT Mechanix - Detroit Mechanics</title>
    <!-- Bootstrap CSS -->
    <link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.0/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css" rel="stylesheet">
    <style>
        /* Basic styling */
        .shop-title {
            font-size: 2.5rem;
            color: #4a90e2;
            margin-bottom: 2rem;
        }

        .hero-content {
            text-align: center;
            padding: 4rem 1rem;
        }

        .services-grid {
            display: grid;
            gap: 2rem;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr));
        }

        .service-card {
            background: #333;
            padding: 2rem;
            border-radius: 10px;
            transition: transform 0.3s ease;
        }

        .service-card:hover {
            transform: translateY(-5px);
        }

        .contact-form {
            background: #333;
            padding: 2rem;
            border-radius: 10px;
        }

        /* Hover effects */
        .hover effect {
            border-color: #4a90e2 !important;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <!-- Navigation -->
    <nav class="navbar navbar-expand-lg navbar-dark bg-dark">
        <div class="container-fluid">
            <a class="navbar-brand" href="#">DT Mechanix</a>
            <button class="navbar-toggler" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#navbarNav">
                <span class="navbar-toggler-icon"></span>
            </button>
            <div class="collapse navbar-collapse" id="navbarNav">
                <ul class="navbar-nav ms-auto">
                    <li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="#">Home</a></li>
                    <li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="#">Services</a></li>
                    <li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="#">Contact</a></li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </nav>

    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <section class="hero">
        <div class="hero-content">
            <h1 class="shop-title">Professional Mechanic Services in Detroit</h1>
            <p>Specializing in car repairs, maintenance, and service in the heart of Detroit.</p>
            <button class="btn btn-primary" data-bs-toggle="modal" data-bs-target="#contactFormModal">
                Book an Estimate
            </button>
            <div class="DT-code">DTCODE: DTM</div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Services Section -->
    <section class="services">
        <div class="container-fluid">
            <h2 class="text-center mb-5">Our Services</h2>
            <div class="row services-grid">
                <div class="col-md-4 service-card">
                    <h3 class="card-title hover:underline">Engine Repairs</h3>
                    <p>Trauma from accidents? We've got you covered!</p>
                    <button class="btn btn-primary service-card:hover:underline" type="button" data-bs-toggle="modal" data-bs-target="#contactFormModal">
                        Learn More
                    </button>
                </div>
                <!-- Add more service cards as needed -->
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Contact Form -->
    <section class="contact-form">
        <div class="container-fluid">
            <h2 class="text-center mb-5">Contact Us</h2>
            <form id="contactForm" class="mt-4 bg-dark">
                <div class="row">
                    <div class="col-md-6">
                        <label for="name" class="form-label">Name *</label>
                        <input type="text" class="form-control" id="name" name="name" required>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-6">
                        <label for="email" class="form-label">Email *"></label>
                        <input type="email" class="form-control" id="email" name="email" required>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-6">
                        <label for="message" class="form-label">Message</label>
                        <textarea class="form-control" id="message" name="message" rows="4"></textarea>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary w-100">Send Message</button>
            </form>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Footer -->
    <footer class="bg-dark mt-5 py-3">
        <div class="container-fluid text-center">
            <p>&copy; 2024 DT Mechanix. All rights reserved.</p>
        </div>
    </footer>

    <script src="https://code.jquery.com/jquery-3.6.0.min.js"></script>
    <script>
        $(document).ready(function() {
            $('#contactForm').on('submit', function(e) {
                e.preventDefault();
                // Here you would typically send the form data to a server
                // For this example, we'll just show a success message
                alert('Message sent successfully! We will get back to you soon.');
                setTimeout(() => {
                    alert('Message sent successfully!');
                }, 2000);
            });
        });
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

This example includes:

1. A responsive navigation bar with logo and menu items
2. A hero section with a call-to-action button
3. A services section with hover effects on cards
4. A contact form with validation
5. Responsive design using Bootstrap's grid system
6. Hover animations and transitions
7. Dark theme colors suitable for Detroit aesthetic

Features:
- Responsive layout that works on mobile and desktop
- Smooth hover animations
- Contact form with basic validation
- Professional color scheme matching Detroit aesthetics
- Fake data and examples to demonstrate structure

To use this template:

1. Copy the code into a .html file
2. Make sure you have an internet connection (for Bootstrap and jQuery CDN)
3. Open in a web browser

Note: The JavaScript at the bottom is minimal for this example, but you can expand it with actual form submission handling.

You can customize the colors, spacing, and content to match your specific needs or brand guidelines.
